    "body": "<!-- Thanks for contributing to Jetpack! Pick a clear title (\"Sharing: add new Facebook button\") and proceed. -->\n#### Steps to reproduce the issue\n1. Turn on JetPack Sharing buttons and put Facebook button on the page\n2. Set the Button Style to \"Icon + Text\".\n3. Go to the blog home page\n4. Observe network requests from DevTools\n#### What I expected\n1. No requests made to graph.facebook.com\n#### What happened instead\n1. 3 requests made to graph.facebook.com\n#### Note\n\nThis can be workaround by adding a `jetpack_sharing_counts` filter, added back in 2004. However itself is a bug that should be corrected. \n\nIt's a privacy issue too, since we are essentially ended up allowing Facebook to track it's user on every WordPress blog post s/he reads (assuming 3rd-party cookie is not blocked).\n",
